              "text": "Because **\"Glenwood Pool\"** can refer to several different well-known locations across the United States, here is a breakdown of the most prominent ones:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Resort Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" in the world. \n* **What it is:** Home to the **world's largest mineral hot springs pool**, which has been drawing visitors since 1888. \n* **Key Features:** \n  * **The Grand Pool:** Spans over two city blocks and is kept at a comfortable 90\u00b0F\u201393\u00b0F (32\u00b0C\u201334\u00b0C).\n  * **The Therapy Pool:** A hotter soaking pool kept at a restorative 104\u00b0F (40\u00b0C).\n  * **Yampah Mineral Baths & Sopris Splash Zone:** Newer family-friendly splash areas and upscale mineral baths.\n* **Access:** Open to the public year-round (except for scheduled maintenance days). You can buy day passes, and lodge guests get complimentary pool access.\n* **Address:** 401 N River St, Glenwood Springs, CO 81601.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Glenwood Pool / Glenwood Recreation Club (Silver Spring, Maryland)\nA highly popular local community pool in the Washington, D.C. suburbs.\n* **What it is:** A historic, private cooperative swim club set among the trees in the Forest Glen neighborhood. It has been operating since 1953.\n* **Key Features:** Active swim and dive teams (the Glenwood Tigers), early bird swim hours, and popular neighborhood social events.\n* **Access:** Membership-based. Due to high demand, there is typically a multi-year waiting list to join.\n* **Address:** 10012 Gardiner Ave, Silver Spring, MD 20902.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Glenwood Pool (Columbus, Ohio)\nA state-of-the-art public pool managed by the Columbus Recreation and Parks Department.\n* **What it is:** Located in Glenwood Park on Columbus's west side, this facility underwent a massive, multi-million dollar redesign and celebrated its grand reopening in July 2023.\n* **Key Features:** A brand-new 6-lane (25-yard) pool, a diving pool with 1-meter boards, water slides, a plunge pool, and an activity pool with a zero-entry edge.\n* **Access:** Open to the public during the summer. Admission requires a free Columbus Recreation and Parks Leisure Card plus a daily admission fee or seasonal pass.\n* **Address:** 1888 Fairmont Ave, Columbus, OH 43223.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia)\nA neighborhood pool serving a walkable, eco-friendly community.\n* **What it is:** A private community pool located in the New Urbanist \"Glenwood Park\" neighborhood on the east side of Atlanta.\n* **Key Features:** A 6-lane, Junior Olympic-sized saline pool with an integrated shallow wading area, a kids' water play fountain, and the local Glenwood Park Piranhas summer swim team.\n* **Access:** Membership is reserved primarily for residents living within the Glenwood Park neighborhood boundary. \n* **Address:** 943 North Ormewood Park Drive SE, Atlanta, GA 30316.\n\n***\n\n*If you are looking for specific hours, pricing, or registration details for one of these pools, please let me know which location you are interested in!*",
